/* ---------------- Çeviri ---------------- */
{kat:"Çeviri", s:"The findings have serious implications for public health policy.", se:["Bulgular, halk sağlığı politikası açısından ciddi sonuçlar doğurmaktadır.","Bulgular, halk sağlığı politikasının ciddiyetini ortaya koymaktadır.","Halk sağlığı politikası ciddi bulgulara dayandırılmaktadır.","Bulguların halk sağlığı politikasıyla ciddi bir ilgisi bulunmamaktadır.","Halk sağlığı politikası bu bulguları yeterince ciddiye almamaktadır."], d:0, ac:"<b>implications for</b> = -e yönelik sonuçlar/doğurgular. Cümle bir olumsuzluk ya da 'ciddiye almama' anlamı taşımıyor."},
{kat:"Çeviri", s:"Unless funding is increased, the project will have to be abandoned.", se:["Fon artırılsa bile projeden vazgeçilecektir.","Fon artırılmadıkça projeden vazgeçilmek zorunda kalınacaktır.","Proje terk edilirse fon artırılacaktır.","Fon artırıldığı için proje sürdürülebilecektir.","Projeden vazgeçilmesi, fonun artırılmasına bağlıdır."], d:1, ac:"<b>Unless</b> = -medikçe / -mezse. Ayrıca 'will have to be abandoned' hem zorunluluk hem edilgenlik taşır."},
{kat:"Çeviri", s:"Kentin nüfusu son yirmi yılda iki katına çıktı.", se:["The city's population has doubled over the past two decades.","The city's population will double in the next two decades.","The city has had a population of two million for twenty years.","The population of the city doubles every two decades.","Two decades ago, the city's population was twice as large."], d:0, ac:"'son yirmi yılda' → <b>over the past two decades</b> ve Present Perfect ('has doubled'): geçmişte başlayıp bugüne uzanan değişim."},
{kat:"Çeviri", s:"Bu tür kararlar alınmadan önce uzmanlara danışılmalıdır.", se:["Experts should be consulted before such decisions are taken.","Experts have consulted specialists before taking such decisions.","Such decisions are usually taken by consulting experts.","Before consulting experts, such decisions must be taken.","Experts must decide before any such consultation takes place."], d:0, ac:"Türkçe cümlede iki edilgen yapı var: 'danışılmalıdır' → should be consulted, 'alınmadan önce' → before ... are taken."},
{kat:"Çeviri", s:"Although the treatment relieves the symptoms, it does not cure the disease.", se:["Tedavi belirtileri hafifletse de hastalığı iyileştirmez.","Tedavi hastalığı iyileştirir ancak belirtileri gidermez.","Belirtiler hafiflediği için hastalık iyileşmiş sayılır.","Tedavi ne belirtileri hafifletir ne de hastalığı iyileştirir.","Hastalık iyileşmedikçe belirtiler hafiflemez."], d:0, ac:"'Although' → '-se de'. B şıkkı iki yüklemin yerini değiştirdiği için anlamı tersine çevirir; YDS'de en sık kurulan tuzaktır."},
{kat:"Çeviri", s:"Şirket, çalışanlarının çoğunu işten çıkarmak zorunda kaldı.", se:["The company had to lay off most of its employees.","The company decided not to dismiss any of its employees.","Most of the company's employees resigned of their own accord.","The company was forced to take on more employees.","Most employees had to leave the company voluntarily."], d:0, ac:"'zorunda kaldı' → <b>had to</b> (geçmişte mecburiyet); 'işten çıkarmak' → lay off / dismiss. C ve E şıkları çalışanların kendi isteğiyle ayrıldığını söylüyor, bu yanlış."},

/* ---------------- Bağlaç (ek sorular) ---------------- */
{kat:"Bağlaç", s:"The new drug reduces symptoms quickly; ----, it does nothing to address the underlying condition.", se:["however","therefore","likewise","hence","thereby"], d:0, ac:"<b>however</b> = ancak. Olumlu bir bilgiden sınırlayıcı bir olumsuza geçiliyor; diğer dört şık da sonuç ya da benzerlik bildiriyor."},
{kat:"Bağlaç", s:"---- the committee had approved the budget, work on the site began immediately.", se:["Once","Unless","Whereas","In case","Despite"], d:0, ac:"<b>Once</b> = -ınca, bir kez ... olduğunda. Onay verilmesi, işin başlamasının ön koşulu ve öncülüdür."},
{kat:"Bağlaç", s:"The material is remarkably light ---- extremely strong, which makes it ideal for aircraft.", se:["yet","so","for","nor","or"], d:0, ac:"<b>yet</b> = ama, yine de. Hafiflik ile sağlamlık beklenmedik bir birliktelik olduğu için karşıtlık bağlacı gerekir."},
{kat:"Bağlaç", s:"---- the delay, all passengers were offered a full refund.", se:["Owing to","Although","Even though","Whereas","Since"], d:0, ac:"Boşluktan sonra isim öbeği ('the delay') var → <b>Owing to</b>. Diğer dört şık tam cümle ister."},
{kat:"Bağlaç", s:"The scheme failed ---- it had been carefully planned and generously funded.", se:["even though","because","so that","as if","in case"], d:0, ac:"<b>even though</b> = -mesine rağmen. İyi planlanmış olmasına <i>karşın</i> başarısız olması ödünleme ilişkisidir."},
{kat:"Bağlaç", s:"Water levels continued to rise; ----, the villages downstream were evacuated.", se:["accordingly","nevertheless","conversely","otherwise","alternatively"], d:0, ac:"<b>accordingly</b> = buna göre, bu nedenle. İkinci cümle birincinin doğrudan sonucudur."},
{kat:"Bağlaç", s:"---- reducing costs, the new process also cuts water consumption by half.", se:["In addition to","In addition","Moreover","Furthermore","Besides that"], d:0, ac:"Boşluktan sonra V-ing ('reducing') geldiği için edat işlevli <b>In addition to</b> gerekir; diğerleri cümle zarfıdır ve fiilimsi alamaz."},
{kat:"Bağlaç", s:"You should back up your files regularly; ----, a single hardware fault could destroy years of work.", se:["otherwise","therefore","meanwhile","similarly","in short"], d:0, ac:"<b>otherwise</b> = aksi takdirde. Bir öğüdün ardından, uyulmazsa doğacak olumsuz sonucu bağlar."},
{kat:"Bağlaç", s:"The two designs are almost identical ---- the second one uses a lighter frame.", se:["except that","except","besides","apart","rather"], d:0, ac:"Boşluktan sonra tam cümle var → <b>except that</b>. Yalın 'except' isim öbeği alır: <i>except the frame</i>."},
{kat:"Bağlaç", s:"---- the survey was conducted entirely online, older respondents are probably underrepresented.", se:["Since","Despite","In spite of","Whereas","Unless"], d:0, ac:"<b>Since</b> burada neden bildirir (-dığı için). Anketin çevrim içi olması, yaşlıların az temsil edilmesinin sebebidir."},
{kat:"Bağlaç", s:"The first results were inconclusive; ----, the team decided to repeat the entire experiment.", se:["consequently","however","nevertheless","in contrast","by comparison"], d:0, ac:"<b>consequently</b> = sonuç olarak. Belirsiz sonuç, deneyin tekrarlanmasının nedenidir."},
{kat:"Bağlaç", s:"Tourism brings much-needed income to the region; ----, it puts serious pressure on fragile ecosystems.", se:["on the other hand","on the contrary","as a result","in other words","for instance"], d:0, ac:"<b>on the other hand</b> = öte yandan; madalyonun diğer yüzünü sunar. 'on the contrary' önceki iddiayı <i>reddederdi</i>, burada reddedilen bir şey yok."},
{kat:"Bağlaç", s:"The device continued to function normally ---- being submerged for over an hour.", se:["despite","although","even though","whereas","since"], d:0, ac:"Boşluktan sonra V-ing ('being') var → <b>despite</b>. Diğer şıklar özne-yüklemli cümle ister."},
{kat:"Bağlaç", s:"---- the last fluent speaker dies, a language is effectively gone.", se:["Once","Unless","In case","So that","Whereas"], d:0, ac:"<b>Once</b> = -dığı anda. Son konuşurun ölümü, dilin yok oluşunun eşiğidir."},
{kat:"Bağlaç", s:"He did not attend the meeting, ---- did he send an apology.", se:["nor","or","neither","either","so"], d:0, ac:"<b>nor</b> olumsuz ekleme yapar ve ardından devrik yapı gelir ('did he send'). 'neither' bu konumda bağlaç olarak kullanılmaz."},
{kat:"Bağlaç", s:"The theory is elegant and internally consistent; ----, it fails to account for several well-documented observations.", se:["nonetheless","thus","hence","accordingly","likewise"], d:0, ac:"<b>nonetheless</b> = yine de. Övgünün ardından gelen eleştiri zıtlık ilişkisidir; diğer dördü sonuç veya benzerlik bildirir."},
{kat:"Bağlaç", s:"Emissions must be cut sharply ---- the 2050 target is to be met.", se:["if","unless","despite","whereas","although"], d:0, ac:"<b>if</b>. 'unless' seçilirse anlam tersine döner: hedefe ulaşılmayacaksa kesinti gerekir — bu mantıksızdır."},

/* ---------------- Cümle Tamamlama ---------------- */
{kat:"Cümle Tamamlama", s:"Because the samples had been stored at the wrong temperature, ----.", se:["the laboratory had to repeat the entire analysis","the results were considered unusually reliable","the researchers published them without further checks","storage conditions rarely affect this kind of sample","the equipment had been working perfectly all along"], d:0, ac:"'Because' neden bildirir; ana cümle bu nedenin <b>sonucu</b> olmalı. Yanlış saklanan örnek analizi geçersiz kılar, güvenilir yapmaz."},
{kat:"Cümle Tamamlama", s:"---- unless the government substantially increases funding for public transport.", se:["Traffic congestion in the city will continue to worsen","Traffic congestion in the city has already been solved","The number of private cars has been falling steadily","Public transport was privatised more than a decade ago","Commuters were entirely satisfied with the existing service"], d:0, ac:"<b>unless</b> = -medikçe. Koşul gerçekleşmezse ortaya çıkacak <i>olumsuz</i> bir sonuç gerekir; ayrıca gelecek zaman uyumu aranır."},
{kat:"Cümle Tamamlama", s:"Although the treatment has proved highly effective in laboratory conditions, ----.", se:["it has not yet been tested on human patients","researchers immediately approved it for general use","laboratory conditions are identical to real-world ones","it was withdrawn because it produced no effect at all","no further research on it will ever be necessary"], d:0, ac:"'Although' ödünleme kurar: olumlu bir gerçeğin ardından onu <b>sınırlayan</b> bir bilgi gelir. D şıkkı ilk yarıyla doğrudan çelişiyor."},
{kat:"Cümle Tamamlama", s:"The city council decided to widen the main avenue so that ----.", se:["traffic could flow more freely during rush hours","the number of accidents had increased sharply","it was demolished again the following year","residents had been complaining about noise for years","the project was eventually cancelled on cost grounds"], d:0, ac:"<b>so that</b> amaç bildirir; ardından <i>hedeflenen</i> durum gelir. B ve D neden, C ve E ise sonrasında olan olaylardır."},
{kat:"Cümle Tamamlama", s:"----, scientists still cannot predict earthquakes with any useful precision.", se:["Despite decades of intensive research","Because of decades of intensive research","In order to research the subject for decades","So that research may continue for decades","As a result of increasingly precise predictions"], d:0, ac:"<b>Despite + isim öbeği</b>. Uzun araştırmaya <i>rağmen</i> başarısızlık: ödünleme. B seçilirse araştırma başarısızlığın nedeni olurdu, bu mantıksız."},
{kat:"Cümle Tamamlama", s:"By the time the rescue team finally reached the village, ----.", se:["most of the residents had already been evacuated","most of the residents will have to be evacuated","the residents are being evacuated at this moment","the evacuation is scheduled to begin tomorrow","the team is still preparing to set out"], d:0, ac:"<b>By the time + Simple Past</b> yapısı ana cümlede Past Perfect ister: o andan önce tamamlanmış eylem."},
{kat:"Cümle Tamamlama", s:"If the manuscript had been discovered a century earlier, ----.", se:["our understanding of the period would be very different today","it will completely change our understanding of the period","scholars are still debating whether it is authentic","it must be kept in a temperature-controlled room","almost nobody had ever heard of its existence"], d:0, ac:"<b>Karışık tip koşul:</b> if + had V3 (geçmiş koşul) → would + V1 (bugüne uzanan sonuç). 'today' zarfı bu yapıyı doğruluyor."},
{kat:"Cümle Tamamlama", s:"The species has survived in the region ----.", se:["because its habitat has remained largely undisturbed","despite its habitat has been almost entirely destroyed","in spite of it survives more easily than expected","although the habitat has remained completely undisturbed","so that the surrounding habitat was gradually destroyed"], d:0, ac:"B ve C <b>dilbilgisi hatası</b>: despite / in spite of tam cümle alamaz. D anlamca çelişik (bozulmamış habitat hayatta kalmayı zorlaştırmaz)."},
{kat:"Cümle Tamamlama", s:"----, the factory continued to operate at full capacity.", se:["Even though a third of the workers had gone on strike","Because a third of the workers had gone on strike","Since production had been halted the previous week","So that the workers would go on strike immediately","In order to bring production to a complete stop"], d:0, ac:"Grev normalde üretimi <i>durdurur</i>; buna karşın tam kapasite çalışılması ödünleme ilişkisidir → <b>Even though</b>."},
{kat:"Cümle Tamamlama", s:"Not only did the new policy reduce waiting times, ----.", se:["but it also cut administrative costs significantly","and it increased administrative costs significantly","so it managed to cut administrative costs as well","but also cutting administrative costs significantly","however it cut administrative costs significantly"], d:0, ac:"<b>Not only ... but also</b> ikili kalıptır ve iki yanı paralel olmalıdır: 'did the policy reduce' ↔ 'it also cut'. D şıkkı fiilimsiyle paralelliği bozuyor."},
{kat:"Cümle Tamamlama", s:"The report will not be released to the public ----.", se:["until every claim in it has been independently verified","unless not every claim in it has been verified","despite every claim in it has been verified","so that no claim in it was ever verified","because it was already released to the press last week"], d:0, ac:"<b>until</b> zaman sınırı koyar. B çifte olumsuzlukla anlamı bozuyor, C dilbilgisi hatası, E ilk yarıyla çelişiyor."},
{kat:"Cümle Tamamlama", s:"Having examined all the available evidence, ----.", se:["the judge concluded that the case should be dismissed","the case was concluded by the judge to be dismissed","it was concluded that dismissing the case is better","the evidence was found to be insufficient for a verdict","dismissing the case seemed the only reasonable outcome"], d:0, ac:"<b>Özne uyumu.</b> 'Having examined' eylemini yapan kişi ana cümlenin öznesi olmalıdır. Kanıtı inceleyen bir <i>kişi</i> (the judge) gerekir; dava ya da kanıt inceleme yapamaz."},

/* ---------------- Restatement ---------------- */
{kat:"Restatement", s:"Had the warning been issued earlier, the damage could have been prevented.", se:["The damage could have been avoided if the warning had come sooner.","The warning was issued early, and so the damage was prevented.","The damage was limited thanks to an unusually early warning.","Even a much earlier warning would not have prevented the damage.","The warning came early, but the damage occurred all the same."], d:0, ac:"Devrik Type 3 koşul: <b>Had + özne + V3</b> = If + had V3. Gerçekleşmemiş bir geçmişi anlatır — yani uyarı geç geldi ve hasar oluştu."},
{kat:"Restatement", s:"The project is unlikely to be completed on schedule.", se:["There is little chance that the project will finish on time.","The project will certainly be finished exactly on time.","The project has in fact already been completed on time.","It is absolutely certain that the project will fail.","The schedule was revised to fit the project's needs."], d:0, ac:"<b>unlikely</b> = düşük olasılık. D şıkkındaki 'absolutely certain' olasılığı kesinliğe çevirdiği için aşırı yorumdur."},
{kat:"Restatement", s:"You needn't have brought your own equipment; the lab provides everything.", se:["Bringing your own equipment turned out to be unnecessary, though you did bring it.","You will need to bring your own equipment next time you come.","You were not permitted to bring any equipment of your own.","You forgot to bring the equipment that was needed for the work.","The lab does not provide any of the equipment you need."], d:0, ac:"<b>needn't have V3</b> = yaptı ama gerek yoktu. 'didn't need to' ile karıştırma: o, gerekmiyordu <i>ve yapmadı</i> demektir."},
{kat:"Restatement", s:"No sooner had the announcement been made than criticism began to appear online.", se:["Criticism appeared online immediately after the announcement was made.","Criticism had been appearing online long before the announcement.","The announcement was made in response to earlier online criticism.","The announcement succeeded in preventing any online criticism.","Online criticism caused the announcement to be delayed."], d:0, ac:"<b>No sooner ... than</b> = -er -mez. İki olay arasındaki sırayı ve neredeyse eşzamanlılığı verir."},
{kat:"Restatement", s:"Far from solving the problem, the new regulation made it considerably worse.", se:["The new regulation did not solve the problem; it actually aggravated it.","The new regulation solved the problem completely and permanently.","The problem had already been solved before the regulation appeared.","The regulation had no measurable effect on the problem either way.","The problem would have been far worse without the new regulation."], d:0, ac:"<b>Far from + V-ing</b> = şöyle dursun, bir yana. Beklenen etkinin tam tersinin gerçekleştiğini vurgular."},
{kat:"Restatement", s:"Only after the results were published did the public become aware of the risk.", se:["The public learned of the risk only once the results had been published.","The public had known about the risk well before the results appeared.","The results were published because the public was already aware.","The public never became aware of the risk at any point.","Publishing the results effectively eliminated the risk."], d:0, ac:"<b>Only after ...</b> devrik yapısı, kamuoyunun farkındalığının yayından <i>sonraya</i> kaldığını vurgular."},
{kat:"Restatement", s:"She would rather work independently than join a large research team.", se:["She prefers working on her own to being part of a big team.","She has spent her whole career in large research teams.","She was reluctantly forced to join a large research team.","She strongly dislikes working without close supervision.","She performs much better when she is supervised closely."], d:0, ac:"<b>would rather A than B</b> = B yerine A'yı tercih etmek. Bir tercih bildirir, zorunluluk ya da geçmiş bir durum değil."},
{kat:"Restatement", s:"It was not until the 1960s that the theory gained widespread acceptance.", se:["The theory was not widely accepted before the 1960s.","The theory rapidly lost support during the 1960s.","The theory has been generally accepted since the 19th century.","The theory was decisively rejected in the course of the 1960s.","The theory has still not gained any acceptance today."], d:0, ac:"<b>It was not until X that ...</b> kalıbı, olayın X'ten önce gerçekleşmediğini vurgular; X'te gerçekleştiğini de söyler."},
{kat:"Restatement", s:"Given the limited evidence, the conclusion should be treated with caution.", se:["Because the evidence is scarce, the conclusion must not be accepted too readily.","Since the evidence is abundant, the conclusion can be considered reliable.","The conclusion ought to be rejected outright without further discussion.","More evidence would actually make the conclusion less trustworthy.","Caution becomes unnecessary precisely when evidence is limited."], d:0, ac:"<b>Given</b> = göz önüne alındığında (neden). 'with caution' ihtiyat ister, tamamen reddetmeyi değil — C aşırı yorumdur."},
{kat:"Restatement", s:"Hardly anyone expected the reform to succeed, yet it did.", se:["Almost no one predicted the reform's success, but it succeeded anyway.","Practically everyone was confident that the reform would succeed.","The reform failed in spite of widespread optimism about it.","The reform was abandoned before it could ever be tested.","Nobody had any interest in whether the reform succeeded."], d:0, ac:"<b>Hardly anyone</b> = neredeyse hiç kimse (olumsuz anlam). 'yet it did' ise reformun yine de başardığını söyler."},
{kat:"Restatement", s:"The company would have gone bankrupt but for the government loan.", se:["The company avoided bankruptcy only because it received a government loan.","The company went bankrupt in spite of receiving a government loan.","The government refused to lend any money to the struggling company.","The company turned out not to need the government loan after all.","The government loan was what ultimately caused the bankruptcy."], d:0, ac:"<b>but for + isim</b> = olmasaydı. Kredi geldi ve iflası önledi; gerçekleşmemiş olan iflastır."},
{kat:"Restatement", s:"Little did the researchers realise how much their findings would change the field.", se:["The researchers had no idea at the time how influential their findings would prove.","The researchers were fully aware of the impact their findings would have.","The researchers deliberately exaggerated the importance of their findings.","The findings turned out to have almost no influence on the field.","The researchers changed the field without ever publishing their findings."], d:0, ac:"<b>Little did + özne + V1</b> devrik yapısı 'hiç farkında değildi' anlamı taşır; sonradan büyük etki doğduğunu da ima eder."},

/* ---------------- Paragraf Tamamlama ---------------- */
{kat:"Paragraf Tamamlama", metin:"----. For instance, a single mature tree can absorb tens of kilograms of carbon dioxide each year, while also filtering dust from the air and providing shade that lowers street temperatures. These benefits accumulate: a street lined with trees is measurably cooler and cleaner than an identical street without them.",
 s:"Paragrafın başına hangi cümle gelmelidir?", se:["Trees provide a range of benefits that are easy to overlook in a city","Cutting down urban trees has very few consequences for city dwellers","Most large cities have no trees at all in their central districts","Carbon dioxide is the only pollutant that affects air quality in cities","Shade from trees is entirely unnecessary in temperate climates"], d:0, ac:"Boşluktan sonra <b>For instance</b> geliyor; yani ilk cümle, örneklerin dayanacağı <i>genel bir iddia</i> olmalı. Sayılan örneklerin hepsi ağacın faydası."},
{kat:"Paragraf Tamamlama", metin:"The earliest maps were not attempts to represent the world accurately. ----. A medieval European map might place Jerusalem at the centre and distort every coastline around it, not through ignorance but through conviction. Accuracy became the dominant aim only when maps began to serve navigation and trade.",
 s:"Boşluğa hangi cümle gelmelidir?", se:["They were statements about what mattered, arranged according to belief rather than measurement","They were drawn with instruments far more precise than any available today","Navigation was in fact the primary purpose of every map ever produced","Most of these early maps have survived intact into the present day","They were produced exclusively by professionally trained surveyors"], d:0, ac:"Boşluk, ilk cümledeki olumsuzlamanın <b>olumlu karşılığını</b> vermeli; sonraki cümledeki 'not through ignorance but through conviction' de inanç vurgusunu doğruluyor."},
{kat:"Paragraf Tamamlama", metin:"Rivers rarely flow in straight lines. Even across flat ground a channel begins to curve, and once a curve forms, water on the outer bank speeds up and erodes it further while the inner bank collects sediment. ----. Left alone, a meander eventually loops so far that the river cuts across its own neck, abandoning the bend as an oxbow lake.",
 s:"Boşluğa hangi cümle gelmelidir?", se:["The curve therefore deepens itself, and the process feeds on its own effects","As a result, the river gradually straightens itself out over time","Sediment is removed equally from both banks during this process","Flat ground is the only place where a river can flow perfectly straight","Oxbow lakes generally form long before any meander develops"], d:0, ac:"Önceki cümle bir <b>kendini besleyen döngü</b> anlatıyor; sonraki cümle bu döngünün sonucunu veriyor. B akışa ters, C önceki cümleyle çelişik."},
{kat:"Paragraf Tamamlama", metin:"For most of human history, sleep was not a single unbroken block. Records from medieval Europe describe a 'first sleep' and a 'second sleep', separated by an hour or two of wakefulness in the middle of the night. People used that interval to pray, talk or simply lie thinking. ----.",
 s:"Paragrafın sonuna hangi cümle gelmelidir?", se:["The consolidated eight-hour night we treat as natural appears to be a relatively recent habit","This same pattern has continued unchanged in every society right up to the present","Medieval people therefore slept considerably fewer hours in total than we do","Artificial lighting had no discernible effect on how people organised their nights","There is virtually no written evidence about sleep before the modern era"], d:0, ac:"Sonuç cümlesi, anlatılan tarihsel örneğin <b>bugüne bakan çıkarımını</b> vermeli. E paragraftaki 'records ... describe' ifadesiyle doğrudan çelişiyor."},
{kat:"Paragraf Tamamlama", metin:"Language death is rarely sudden. ----. Children stop learning the language at home, then adults use it only with the oldest generation, and finally it survives in a handful of phrases and place names. By the time anyone declares it extinct, the decisive shift has usually happened decades earlier.",
 s:"Boşluğa hangi cümle gelmelidir?", se:["It happens through a slow narrowing of the situations in which a language is used","It usually results from a single catastrophic event affecting all its speakers at once","Most languages disappear within a year of losing their last fluent speaker","Place names are always the very first part of a language to be lost","Children are generally the last group of speakers to abandon a dying language"], d:0, ac:"İlk cümle 'ani değildir' diyor; boşluk bunun <b>olumlu açılımı</b> olmalı ve ardından gelen aşamalı süreci başlatmalı. B ilk cümleyle, E sonraki cümleyle çelişiyor."},
{kat:"Paragraf Tamamlama", metin:"Placebos can work even when patients know they are taking them. In several trials, participants who were openly told that their pills contained no active ingredient still reported significant relief from pain and fatigue. ----. What seems to matter is the ritual of treatment itself — the appointment, the explanation, the act of taking something.",
 s:"Boşluğa hangi cümle gelmelidir?", se:["This finding is hard to reconcile with the assumption that deception is essential to the effect","These results confirmed that patients must always be deceived for a placebo to work","Such trials demonstrate that pain and fatigue are largely imaginary conditions","Active ingredients are therefore irrelevant in every branch of modern medicine","No researcher has ever attempted to run an open-label placebo trial"], d:0, ac:"Boşluk, anlatılan bulgunun <b>neden şaşırtıcı olduğunu</b> söylemeli; sonraki cümle de alternatif açıklamayı sunuyor. B bulguyla, E ilk iki cümleyle çelişiyor."},

/* ---------------- Anlam Bütünlüğünü Bozan Cümle ---------------- */
{kat:"Anlamı Bozan Cümle", metin:"(I) Coral reefs cover less than one per cent of the ocean floor. (II) Nevertheless, they support roughly a quarter of all known marine species. (III) This extraordinary density makes them among the most valuable ecosystems on Earth. (IV) Deep-sea trenches, by contrast, remain almost entirely unexplored by researchers. (V) Their loss would therefore affect far more species than their small area suggests.",
 s:"Anlam bütünlüğünü bozan cümle hangisidir?", se:["IV","I","II","III","V"], d:0, ac:"Paragraf baştan sona <b>mercan resifleri</b> üzerine kurulu. IV derin deniz çukurlarına geçiyor ve V'teki 'Their' zamirinin öncülünü de bozuyor."},
{kat:"Anlamı Bozan Cümle", metin:"(I) The printing press spread across Europe within a few decades of its invention. (II) By 1500, presses were operating in more than two hundred cities. (III) The resulting fall in book prices made written texts available to a far wider public. (IV) Literacy rates rose steadily throughout the century that followed. (V) Most medieval manuscripts were written on parchment made from animal skin.",
 s:"Anlam bütünlüğünü bozan cümle hangisidir?", se:["V","I","II","III","IV"], d:0, ac:"I–IV matbaanın yayılışı ve sonuçlarını zincirleme anlatıyor. V, matbaa öncesi el yazmalarının <b>malzemesine</b> geçerek zinciri kırıyor."},
{kat:"Anlamı Bozan Cümle", metin:"(I) Bees navigate using a combination of sunlight and remembered landmarks. (II) When the sun is hidden, they rely on patterns of polarised light in the sky. (III) Honey has been used as a food preservative for thousands of years. (IV) Experienced foragers also memorise prominent features close to the hive. (V) These overlapping systems make bee navigation remarkably reliable.",
 s:"Anlam bütünlüğünü bozan cümle hangisidir?", se:["III","I","II","IV","V"], d:0, ac:"Paragrafın konusu arıların <b>yön bulması</b>. III balın gıda koruyucu olarak kullanımına geçiyor — aynı canlı, farklı konu."},
{kat:"Anlamı Bozan Cümle", metin:"(I) Sleep deprivation impairs attention long before people notice any change in themselves. (II) In one study, participants who had slept five hours rated their own alertness as entirely normal. (III) Their performance on reaction tests, however, had fallen sharply. (IV) This gap between perceived and actual ability is what makes tiredness so dangerous. (V) Caffeine was first isolated from coffee beans in 1819.",
 s:"Anlam bütünlüğünü bozan cümle hangisidir?", se:["V","I","II","III","IV"], d:0, ac:"I–IV tek bir iddiayı kuruyor: kişi kendi yorgunluğunu fark etmez. V kafeinin <b>keşif tarihine</b> geçiyor; paragrafın argümanına hiçbir katkısı yok."},
{kat:"Anlamı Bozan Cümle", metin:"(I) Venice has been sinking slowly for many centuries. (II) Groundwater extraction during the twentieth century accelerated the process considerably. (III) Rising sea levels have since compounded the problem. (IV) The city now floods several times each winter. (V) Venetian glassmaking has long been concentrated on the island of Murano.",
 s:"Anlam bütünlüğünü bozan cümle hangisidir?", se:["V","I","II","III","IV"], d:0, ac:"I–IV Venedik'in <b>batması</b> üzerine nedensel bir zincir. V cam üretimine geçiyor — şehir aynı, konu değil."},
{kat:"Anlamı Bozan Cümle", metin:"(I) Most languages borrow words from their neighbours. (II) English alone has absorbed vocabulary from more than three hundred languages. (III) Borrowing usually occurs when speakers encounter unfamiliar objects or ideas. (IV) Grammatical structures, by contrast, are borrowed far less often. (V) The modern English alphabet contains twenty-six letters.",
 s:"Anlam bütünlüğünü bozan cümle hangisidir?", se:["V","I","II","III","IV"], d:0, ac:"Konu <b>sözcük ödünçlemesi</b>. IV bile karşıtlık kurarak konuya bağlı kalıyor; V ise alfabedeki harf sayısına atlıyor."},
{kat:"Anlamı Bozan Cümle", metin:"(I) Antibiotic resistance develops when some bacteria survive exposure to a drug. (II) The survivors then pass their resistance on to the next generation. (III) Overprescription accelerates this process considerably. (IV) The first hospital in the region was built in 1878. (V) Within a few years, a once-effective drug can become almost useless.",
 s:"Anlam bütünlüğünü bozan cümle hangisidir?", se:["IV","I","II","III","V"], d:0, ac:"I, II, III ve V direnç gelişiminin <b>nedensel zincirini</b> kuruyor. IV bir hastanenin yapım tarihi — tamamen ilgisiz."},
{kat:"Anlamı Bozan Cümle", metin:"(I) Urban green spaces lower surrounding air temperatures by several degrees. (II) They also absorb rainwater that would otherwise overwhelm drainage systems. (III) Residents living close to parks report measurably lower levels of stress. (IV) City authorities are therefore increasingly treating parks as infrastructure rather than decoration. (V) Most public parks charge an entrance fee during the summer months.",
 s:"Anlam bütünlüğünü bozan cümle hangisidir?", se:["V","I","II","III","IV"], d:0, ac:"I–III parkların faydalarını sıralıyor, IV bunlardan bir <b>sonuç</b> çıkarıyor. V ise ücretlendirmeye geçiyor ve akışı bozuyor."},

/* ---------------- Diyalog Tamamlama ---------------- */
{kat:"Diyalog", metin:"Researcher: Have you had a chance to look at the revised figures?\nAssistant: I have, but something doesn't add up in the third column.\nResearcher: ----\nAssistant: It looks like the totals were calculated before the last two entries were added.",
 s:"Boşluğa ne gelmelidir?", se:["What exactly seems to be the problem?","I'm very glad everything is in order, then.","Let's not worry about those figures at all.","Why did you refuse to check them for me?","The third column was actually removed last week."], d:0, ac:"Asistan bir sorun olduğunu söylüyor, sonraki replikte sorunu <b>açıklıyor</b>. Aradaki soru, o açıklamayı isteyen bir soru olmalı."},
{kat:"Diyalog", metin:"Student: I'm thinking of taking the exam in September rather than in June.\nAdvisor: ----\nStudent: Mainly because I'd have another three months to work on my reading speed.",
 s:"Boşluğa ne gelmelidir?", se:["May I ask what's behind that decision?","Unfortunately, the exam isn't offered in September.","You have clearly made up your mind already.","Reading speed isn't actually tested on this exam.","I took the exam myself many years ago."], d:0, ac:"Öğrenci 'Mainly because...' diye yanıt veriyor; yani boşlukta bir <b>gerekçe sorusu</b> olmalı. B ve D öğrencinin cevabıyla çelişir."},
{kat:"Diyalog", metin:"Tenant: The heating hasn't been working properly since Tuesday.\nLandlord: I'm sorry to hear that. Have you tried resetting the boiler?\nTenant: ----\nLandlord: In that case I'll send an engineer round tomorrow morning.",
 s:"Boşluğa ne gelmelidir?", se:["Twice, but it switches itself off again after a few minutes.","No, the heating has actually been working perfectly all week.","I'd honestly rather not discuss the boiler at all.","Yes, and it has been running normally ever since.","An engineer came last month for a completely different problem."], d:0, ac:"Ev sahibi 'In that case' diyerek <b>teknisyen gönderiyor</b>; demek ki kiracı denediğini ama sorunun sürdüğünü söylemiş olmalı. D'de sorun çözülmüş olurdu."},
{kat:"Diyalog", metin:"Colleague: Are you going to the conference in Ankara next month?\nYou: ----\nColleague: That's a shame — there are two sessions on your exact research area.",
 s:"Boşluğa ne gelmelidir?", se:["I'd like to, but I've already committed to teaching that week.","Yes, I've booked my train ticket and my hotel already.","Of course — I never miss that particular conference.","I'm actually presenting the opening paper on the Friday.","I'll be there for the whole of the week, in fact."], d:0, ac:"'That's a shame' bir <b>olumsuz yanıta</b> verilen tepkidir. Diğer dört şıkta da katılım olumlu olduğu için tepki anlamsız kalır."},
{kat:"Diyalog", metin:"Editor: The article is strong, but it runs about eight hundred words too long.\nAuthor: ----\nEditor: The historical background, I think. Most of our readers will know it already.",
 s:"Boşluğa ne gelmelidir?", se:["Which section would you suggest I cut?","I don't believe length is ever really a problem.","Then I'll add another section on methodology.","The article is exactly the right length as it stands.","I'd rather submit it to a different journal instead."], d:0, ac:"Editörün yanıtı bir <b>bölüm adı</b>; öyleyse soru 'hangi bölümü keseyim' olmalı. C ve D metni uzatır ya da sorunu reddeder."},
{kat:"Diyalog", metin:"Passenger: Excuse me, is this the platform for the Izmir train?\nAttendant: It was, but the departure has been moved to platform six.\nPassenger: ----\nAttendant: You've got about twelve minutes, so there's no need to run.",
 s:"Boşluğa ne gelmelidir?", se:["Do I have enough time to get over there?","Then I'll just wait here until it arrives.","I wasn't actually planning to travel today.","Platform six is where I've just come from.","Has the train already left without me, then?"], d:0, ac:"Görevli <b>kalan süreyi</b> söylüyor; öyleyse yolcu zamanın yetip yetmediğini sormuş olmalı."},
{kat:"Diyalog", metin:"Doctor: How have you been sleeping since we changed the dose?\nPatient: ----\nDoctor: That's encouraging. Let's keep it at this level for another month.",
 s:"Boşluğa ne gelmelidir?", se:["Much better — I'm waking up perhaps once a night instead of four times.","Worse than ever, unfortunately; I barely sleep at all now.","I stopped taking the medication altogether a fortnight ago.","I haven't noticed the slightest difference, to be honest.","I'd like to increase the dose considerably, if possible."], d:0, ac:"'That's encouraging' ve dozun <b>aynı kalması</b> kararı, ancak olumlu bir gelişme bildirildiğinde anlamlıdır."},
{kat:"Diyalog", metin:"Manager: We need someone to present the quarterly results to the board on Thursday.\nEmployee: ----\nManager: Don't worry about that — I'll go through the slides with you beforehand.",
 s:"Boşluğa ne gelmelidir?", se:["I'd be willing, though I've never presented to the board before.","I'm afraid I'll be on leave for the whole of next month.","I presented them last quarter and it went perfectly well.","Thursday is the only day I'm definitely not available.","I don't think these results are worth presenting at all."], d:0, ac:"Yönetici bir <b>endişeyi gideriyor</b> ('Don't worry about that') ve hazırlık desteği öneriyor; öyleyse çalışan kabul edip deneyimsizliğini dile getirmiş olmalı."},

/* ---------------- Okuma Parçası ---------------- */
{kat:"Okuma", pid:"p1", s:"Parça esas olarak ne ile ilgilidir?", se:["how a single artefact changed assumptions about ancient Greek technology","the techniques used by sponge divers working in the Aegean Sea","the reasons why the Olympic Games were held every four years","the development of X-ray imaging during the twentieth century","the most common causes of shipwrecks in the ancient Mediterranean"], d:0, ac:"Parçanın son üç cümlesi ana fikri veriyor: mekanizma, Yunan teknolojisine dair yerleşik varsayımın <b>yeniden değerlendirilmesini</b> gerektiriyor. Diğer şıklar metinde geçen ama tali olan ayrıntılar."},
{kat:"Okuma", pid:"p1", s:"According to the passage, the mechanism's true nature became clear ----.", se:["only after X-ray imaging was applied to it in the 1970s","immediately after it was recovered from the sea in 1901","when written records describing the device were discovered","once several similar devices were found elsewhere in Europe","after the shipwreck itself had been completely excavated"], d:0, ac:"Metin açık: 'Only when X-ray imaging was applied in the 1970s did its true nature emerge.' Ayrıca 'For decades it attracted little attention' B'yi eliyor."},
{kat:"Okuma", pid:"p1", s:"It can be inferred from the passage that ----.", se:["some ancient technical knowledge disappeared without being documented","Greek scholars of the period were largely uninterested in astronomy","European gear-cutting developed directly from surviving Greek models","the mechanism was used mainly in religious ceremonies","historians have always held Greek engineering in high regard"], d:0, ac:"Son cümle: gelişmiş bir dişli geleneği 'existed and was then lost, leaving almost no trace in the written record'. Bu doğrudan A'nın çıkarımıdır."},
{kat:"Okuma", pid:"p2", s:"Parçanın ana düşüncesi nedir?", se:["Urban heat is produced by the built environment and hits the poorest residents hardest","Air conditioning is the only genuinely effective response to urban heat","The European heatwave of 2003 was caused by a shortage of city trees","Rural areas are gradually becoming as warm as nearby cities","Concrete absorbs considerably less solar radiation than vegetation does"], d:0, ac:"Parça iki şeyi birlikte kuruyor: ısının <b>nedeni</b> (malzemeler ve yapılaşma) ve <b>eşitsiz dağılımı</b> ('the hottest parts of a city are typically its poorest')."},
{kat:"Okuma", pid:"p2", s:"According to the passage, narrow streets between tall buildings ----.", se:["make it harder for trapped heat to radiate away to the sky","allow cities to cool down faster than the surrounding countryside","increase the rate of evaporation from soil and vegetation","reduce the total amount of solar radiation that is absorbed","are found almost exclusively in the wealthier districts"], d:0, ac:"'Tall buildings compound the effect by trapping heat in narrow streets that radiate poorly to the open sky.' — 'compound' burada etkiyi <i>artırmak</i> demektir."},
{kat:"Okuma", pid:"p2", s:"It is implied in the passage that measures against urban heat ----.", se:["are often not targeted at the districts that would benefit most","have proved completely ineffective wherever they have been tried","are cheaper than air conditioning in absolutely every case","were introduced for the first time after the 2003 heatwave","work only in small rural settlements rather than in cities"], d:0, ac:"Son cümle: önlemler 'rarely concentrated where they would do the most good'. Aynı cümle 'can reduce local temperatures measurably' dediği için B yanlış."},
{kat:"Okuma", pid:"p3", s:"Parça esas olarak ne anlatmaktadır?", se:["how the understanding of bilingualism's effects on children has changed","the most effective methods for teaching a second language at school","why immigrant children tend to perform poorly in national tests","the number of words a typical child learns before adolescence","techniques for measuring sustained attention in young children"], d:0, ac:"Parça 'For much of the twentieth century ... was thought to be harmful' ile başlayıp 'What is no longer disputed' ile bitiyor: baştan sona bir <b>görüş değişimi</b> anlatısı."},
{kat:"Okuma", pid:"p3", s:"According to the passage, the early studies of bilingual children were flawed because they ----.", se:["failed to take account of differences in schooling and income","tested only those children who had already reached adolescence","measured combined vocabulary instead of single-language vocabulary","relied entirely on tasks that had no linguistic content at all","were carried out exclusively on monolingual native speakers"], d:0, ac:"'studies that compared immigrant children with native speakers while ignoring differences in schooling and income' — kusur tam olarak budur."},
{kat:"Okuma", pid:"p3", s:"The author's attitude towards the claimed attention advantage of bilinguals is best described as ----.", se:["cautious — the effect is reported but its size is treated as unsettled","dismissive — the evidence is presented as essentially worthless","enthusiastic — the effect is described as firmly established","hostile — the researchers involved are accused of dishonesty","indifferent — the whole question is treated as unimportant"], d:0, ac:"Yazar etkiyi aktarıyor ('appear to develop') ama hemen ardından 'remains disputed' ve 'failed to replicate' diyor. Ne reddediyor ne benimsiyor: <b>ihtiyatlı</b>."},
{kat:"Okuma", pid:"p4", s:"According to the passage, the German findings were especially alarming because ----.", se:["the losses occurred inside areas that were supposed to be protected","the monitoring had lasted only a very short period of time","the reserves in question contained no flowering plants at all","a single clear cause could be identified for the entire decline","insect numbers in the region had been rising until quite recently"], d:0, ac:"'The figure was startling partly because the sites were protected areas.' Ayrıca izleme 27 yıl sürmüş, yani B yanlış."},
{kat:"Okuma", pid:"p4", s:"The passage suggests that the cause of the insect decline ----.", se:["is probably a combination of several factors rather than a single one","has now been definitively identified as agricultural pesticide use","is entirely unrelated to any form of human activity","lies in the warming of the climate and nothing else","remains completely unexamined by the research community"], d:0, ac:"Dört olası etken sayıldıktan sonra 'it is likely that several act together' deniyor — tek bir neden değil, <b>birleşik etki</b>."},
{kat:"Okuma", pid:"p4", s:"Regarding the link between insect loss and falling farmland bird numbers, the author ----.", se:["notes a close correspondence but stops short of claiming causation","states firmly that insect loss is the direct cause of the bird decline","denies that farmland bird numbers have changed in any way","argues that the birds are themselves causing the insect decline","claims that the two trends have been moving in opposite directions"], d:0, ac:"'Whether that decline is a direct consequence of insect loss is not yet established, but the two curves track each other closely' — <b>korelasyon var, nedensellik iddiası yok</b>."}

